SimonSays TODO

Before 1.0:
* Gaze / Dwell-click: while the dwell window (`F3`) is open its forced mode applies to the whole app, so phrases in other windows can fire by dwell even with dwell saved as Off (REQ-F64). A probe-only override was tried on 2026-10-24 and reverted the same day because gaze dwell stopped working; find out why before retrying (one suspect: it was tested with the saved mode Off, where phrases not dwelling was the intended result). 2026-10-26 diagnosis: the saved mode was indeed Off (`Dwell Mode Selection` = 1 just before that test and right after the revert), and the "works, but after a few seconds" seen after the revert matches the window's 2 s refresh switching the whole app to gaze — so the override most likely worked as designed. To redo it, re-apply the same change and test with the saved mode both Auto (phrases dwell by gaze with the window open and closed) and Off (phrases never dwell; the LOOK probe still does). Simpler alternative: disable the other SimonSays windows while the dwell window is open.
* Translate the English HELP.md changes made since 0.6 into the 17 docs/help/HELP_*.md files, then re-run scripts/build_help_html.ps1. English is ahead in:
  - Structure: the table of contents and section order (everyday use first, editing afterwards), and the new sections Default phrases, Using SimonSays in online meetings, Sounds included with SimonSays, Undoing changes, Where SimonSays keeps your files, and Feedback, support and privacy.
  - Overview: where SimonSays comes from (ALS, general AAC use), free as in freedom, approaching 1.0 and the call for testing, and that it complements rather than replaces full AAC suites (Mind Express, TD Communicator, Grid 3, OptiKey).
  - Editing: "Which editor to use" (the app vs SimonSays Web, ARASAAC pictograms, Fitzgerald Key boards), "Customizing the look (board & category styles)", the PNG/JPG icon-format note, and the new "Restoring the default phrases" flow (open the default phrases board from the boards folder; regedit only as a last resort).
  - Gaze / Dwell-click: the Eye Tracker 5 listed as verified and its 64-bit helper, the `Automatic` note about Tobii background software, `HID eye tracker` using gaze only, the `Lock-on delay` setting and the 500 ms default dwell time, `Move away before dwell can activate again`, the `Save diagnostic report...` button, the "Tobii Eye Tracker 4C software" note on reinstalling Tobii Core 2.13.1.7294, and "What dwell-click works on" (dialog buttons armed after about 0.75 s, the gaze highlight); also "Reporting eye-tracking hardware issues".
  - Everyday use: the "Right-click menu" lines in "Categories window" (including the per-button entries), the renamed `Show quick access buttons and menu` setting, `Exit` asking first in "Tray icon menu", the `Shift + F10` / Menu key, `Space` on `Play>` and `Shift + Insert` shortcuts, and the "could not save" troubleshooting entry.
  - Translated help files also still describe dwell-dialog controls with English labels in backticks (stale at least for Portuguese); use each language's own labels.
* Mirror the Edit / Add dialog and the text preview dialog for Arabic and Hebrew (updateRtlExStyle + ApplyRtlStylesCallback in their WM_INITDIALOG, as Settings and the dwell window do). Their labels are translated, but the layout stays left-to-right (found 2026-11-02, ssbutton.spec.md AC-18).
* Have native speakers review the 0.7 wording before 1.0:
  - Gaze / Dwell-click terminology in Arabic, Basque, Chinese, Hebrew, Hindi, Japanese, Korean and Russian (DWELL_* plus the board-style/delete-all confirmations and the IMPORT_LANGUAGE_* import warnings in include/localized_strings.h; the import warnings use a "File language: <name>" phrasing in these languages because the inserted native name cannot be inflected). The wording follows the conventions already used in the Romance-language tables, but terms like "HID eye tracker", "dwell-click" and "gaze-driven cursor" vary by locale, and this is the setup screen for users who can only operate the app by gaze. Check the Arabic and Hebrew dialog visually too (RTL layout with embedded Latin terms such as HID and Windows). Include the strings added in October 2026: the `Save diagnostic report...` button and its three status messages (DWELL_DUMP_BUTTON_ID, DWELL_STATUS_DUMP_*), the `Lock-on delay` label (DWELL_LOCKON_LABEL_ID), and the Tobii licence (medical use) note in each docs/help/HELP_*.md.
  - The two Conversation phrases added in 0.7 in all 18 languages: the short reaction of surprise or dismay (`Oh dear`, `Vaja!`, `Ene!`, `Oje!`, `عجباً!`, `אוי!`, `अरे!`, `哎呀！`, `おや！`, `이런!`...) and the `Never mind` phrase. Check the labels of the sounds added to `Sounds` in the same pass, above all the `Uh-uh` and `Rimshot` ones (few languages write them) and `Ahem` in Arabic and Hindi, where a descriptive noun was used instead. Interjections rarely translate literally.
  - The European Portuguese interface strings (PORTUGUESE_LOCALIZED_UI_STRINGS in include/localized_strings.h), the Brazilian Portuguese help (docs/help/HELP_pt_BR.md), and both Portuguese default phrase sets (include/default_phrases.h).
  - The ready-made categories in Arabic, Chinese, Hebrew, Hindi, Japanese, Korean and Russian (scripts/extra_boards/yes_no.json, pain_body.json, spelling.json, games.json, questions.json, daily_care.json, hearing_check.json, meeting.json, and the Fitzgerald Key translations in fitzgerald_key.json for Basque and Russian; have a clinician glance at the Daily care wording - suction, cough assist, tube feeding), then re-run scripts/build_extra_boards.ps1. Check also whether isolated letters (Korean jamo, Hindi consonants, Japanese kana) are read sensibly by each language's voice, and the Basque and Galician pain phrases.
* Add tooltips to the main window's quick access buttons (open a board, Settings). SSButton has no tooltip support at all, so this means a new BTN- feature (a TOOLTIPS_CLASS control owned by SSButton) plus two localized strings; today the buttons only carry a window text as their screen-reader name (settings.spec.md SET-N04).

Possible Long Term Goals:
* Settings usable by gaze alone: since 0.7 the push buttons of Settings and the Gaze / Dwell-click window can be dwelled, but their checkboxes, lists and sliders still need a mouse or keyboard. Make them operable by dwell (for example dwell-enabled toggles and +/- steppers).
* Register the SimonSays bar as its own app bar (SHAppBarMessage ABM_NEW) so Windows reserves its space and maximized windows no longer extend under it; and place it clear of the Windows 11 Widgets button (docs/specs/taskbar.spec.md section 18).
* Declare per-monitor DPI awareness. The app declares none, so Windows bitmap-scales it (blurry at 125%+); every layout is in 96-dpi logical pixels and would need scaling.
* Flow fill: option to use the spare room in the category window to fill it with the following categories' phrases (a continuous, gap-free grid) instead of leaving empty space below the selected category's phrases.
* Gaze / Dwell-click: support a 64-bit SimonSays build on machines whose Tobii software only installs a 32-bit engine (4C, PCEye 5), with a 32-bit counterpart of the SimonSaysGaze64 helper. Today the x64 build cannot read those trackers; the shipped 32-bit build reads both kinds.
* Maybe: also set SimonSays' Windows per-app output device (the Volume mixer setting) to the `Sound output` choice, on top of the current routing (docs/specs/sound.spec.md SND-F70), so the PlaySound/MCI fallbacks follow it too and the setting is repaired at startup if Windows resets it. It uses the undocumented Windows.Media.Internal.AudioPolicyConfig factory (IAudioPolicyConfigFactory, Windows 10 21H2+ IID ab3d4648-e242-459f-b02f-541c70306324, SetPersistedDefaultAudioEndpoint for eConsole + eMultimedia); guard it at runtime (RoGetActivationFactory with that exact IID, then write + read back) and keep the current routing alone if either step fails. Tested 2026-10-14: WinMM only honours it in a process started AFTER the setting, so it takes effect from the next launch; while it is set, "Windows default" must open the real system default device explicitly instead of WAVE_MAPPER, or the running app stays on the old device. Clear it when "Windows default" is chosen (uninstalling does not).
* Sound effects library expansion and user customization options.
